<description>
Exchange the two foreground sprite masks while keeping every copy in its original bounding box.

Input structure:
- The dominant color is the background.
- Exactly two foreground colors are present.
- Each foreground color forms one or more copies of a single 8-connected sprite mask.
- The two sprite masks have the same bounding-box size.

Rule:
- Clear every sprite bounding box.
- In each cleared box, draw the other foreground color's template mask in that other color.
- Apply the replacements simultaneously, so all original boxes are cleared before any template is redrawn.

Key insight:
The colors identify two reusable sprite templates, and each template is the replacement shape for the other color.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "two foreground colors on the dominant background; each color forms repeated 8-connected copies of one sprite mask",
  "transform": "clear each sprite bbox and redraw in that bbox the other foreground color's sprite mask using the other color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 9-11 rows x 10-17 cols, background 0
  foreground_colors: exactly 2 distinct non-zero colors
  sprites:
    count_per_color: one color has 1 copy, the other has 1-5 copies; total 3-6 sprites
    bbox_size: both colors share identical bbox size; 2x2, 2x3, or 3x3
    mask: each color has a single 8-connected template mask; the two masks differ
    mask_density: 50-75% of bbox cells filled
    area: 2-6 cells per sprite
    all_copies_identical: all copies of the same color use the exact same mask
  placement:
    min_edge_gap: >=1 cell from grid border for all sprites [observed]
    min_inter_sprite_gap: >=0 bbox gap (no bbox overlap); typically >=1 [observed]
    no_bbox_overlap: sprite bounding boxes must not overlap
  transform:
    rule: swap the two masks -- at each sprite position, clear the bbox and redraw using the OTHER color's template in that OTHER color
    grid_size_unchanged: true

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (9-11 x 10-17), two fg colors, bbox size (2x2 or 2x3 or 3x3).
    2. Generate two distinct 8-connected masks within the bbox; density ~50-75%.
    3. Assign copy counts -- one color gets 1 copy, the other gets 1-5. Total 3-6.
    4. Place all sprites on grid with >=1 cell edge gap and no bbox overlap. This is the output.
    5. Build input by swapping: at each position of color_A copies, draw color_B's mask in color_B; at each color_B position, draw color_A's mask in color_A.
```
